// "an opponent controls [object]" — [`YouControl`]'s opponent-relative twin:
// `Exists(And([And([Permanent, <object>]), ControlledBy(OpponentOf(Ref(You)))]))`:
// what a player controls is a permanent [CR#109.2]. See
// `YouControl` for the shared `Param(0)` object-predicate vocabulary and the
// render note (a hand-written `Exists` render arm, not the generic template
// filler, supplies the indefinite article).
//
// Usage: AnOpponentControls(And([Permanent, Subtype(Island)])).
(
    name: "AnOpponentControls",
    template: "an opponent controls ${0}",
    kinds: [Condition],
    params: [Predicate],
    body: Exists(And([And([Permanent, Param(0)]), ControlledBy(OpponentOf(Ref(You)))])),
)
